Issues Module
Developer Description and Data Structure

Purpose. The Issues Module will record, organize, monitor, and geographically display important concerns affecting
individual barangays or the municipality as a whole. It should allow staff to identify the nature of an issue, who is
affected, where it is occurring, and its current status.
1. Issue Data Entry
Field Description
Barangay Select the barangay affected by the issue. Allow multiple barangays where applicable.
Type of Issue Political, Community, Municipal-Wide, Policy, Infrastructure.
Issue Title or concise description of the specific issue.
Who Are Affected Individuals, groups, sectors, communities, or areas affected by the issue.
Other Details Background, explanation, developments, concerns, and other relevant information.
Status (Recommended) New, Ongoing, For Action, Resolved.
Date Reported (Recommended) Date the issue was first reported or encoded.
Priority (Recommended) Low, Medium, High, Urgent.
2. Municipal-Wide Issues
If an issue affects the entire municipality, staff should be able to select Municipal-Wide / All Barangays. This avoids
encoding the same issue separately for every barangay while still allowing the issue to appear when individual
barangays are viewed.
3. Barangay Issue Summary
When a barangay is clicked on the map, the dashboard should automatically summarize all issues associated with
that barangay.
Summary Metric Example
Total Issues 12
Political 2
Community 4
Municipal-Wide 1
Policy 2
Infrastructure 3
4. Detailed Issue List
Type Issue Who Are Affected Other Details
Infrastructure Damaged Road Residents and motorists Road requires rehabilitation
Community Water Supply 350 households Intermittent water supply

Type Issue Who Are Affected Other Details
Policy New Regulation Local vendors Implementation concerns
5. Map Function
When Issues is selected from the main dashboard, the Mariveles map should remain interactive. The map can
visually represent the number of recorded issues per barangay. Clicking a barangay should open its issue
summary and detailed issue records.
6. Filters
Users should be able to filter the module by All Issues, Political, Community, Municipal-Wide, Policy,
Infrastructure. If the recommended fields are implemented, additional filters should include Status, Priority, and
Date Range.
7. Core Data Logic
Barangay -> Type of Issue -> Issue -> Who Are Affected -> Other Details -> Status -> Date Reported -> Priority
The dashboard automatically generates Total Issues per Barangay + Breakdown by Issue Type + Breakdown by
Status + Detailed Issue List.
8. Recommended Dashboard Summary
At the municipal level, the Issues dashboard may display summary cards for Total Issues, Ongoing Issues, For
Action, Resolved, and Urgent Issues, followed by the interactive Mariveles map and the detailed issue table.